Cadmium zinc telluride (CdZnTe or CZT) is a compound semiconductor material valued for its high electrical resistivity and strong X-ray and gamma-ray detection capabilities at room temperature. Its properties make it suitable for applications in medical imaging, nuclear radiation monitoring, infrared optics, and specialized optoelectronic devices.

What Is the CdZnTe Wafer Market?
The CdZnTe wafer market includes the production and supply of cadmium zinc telluride semiconductor substrates used in radiation detectors and other advanced electronic and optical systems. Unlike conventional detector materials that may require cooling, CdZnTe can support room-temperature operation while providing high energy resolution. Wafer quality, crystal uniformity, defect density, and material purity are important factors influencing product performance.

Key Market Drivers
Rising Demand for Advanced Radiation Detection
Medical imaging, nuclear monitoring, and security screening applications are creating demand for radiation detectors with improved sensitivity and energy resolution. CdZnTe-based detectors can identify X-rays and gamma rays at room temperature, making them useful in specialized diagnostic and radiation monitoring equipment. The report identifies medical imaging as an application accounting for more than 35% of market share.

Expansion of Space Exploration Programs
Space exploration and satellite development are creating opportunities for radiation-resistant semiconductor materials. CdZnTe detectors are being used and investigated in space-based instruments for gamma-ray detection and cosmic radiation monitoring. Continued investment in scientific missions and satellite technologies may support demand for specialized wafer formats.

